\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Expectation and the pairing}
\date{2026-11-13}

\p{The Gaussian expectation #{\langle F\rangle_Q} is the integral
pairing of the law with the observable. Mathematical physics writes
#{\langle O\rangle} or #{\mathbb E[O]}. The glyph is the bracket
already used for the counting inner product. Geometric algebra writes
#{\langle A\rangle} for the scalar part of #{A}. A grade projection
carries its grade, #{\langle A\rangle_r}.}
